  "specification": "teacher-guide-answer-referee-plan-2026-11-16 §6 comparison rules: Arabic-Indic and Western digits; «٫» or «،» between digits is a decimal point and «٬» groups thousands; a «,» between digits is a decimal point unless exactly three digits follow it, and then the context decides: several groups («1,234,567»), a decimal tail («1,250.5»), a «.» decimal elsewhere in the text or a group ending in 0 («1,000», «2,500») group thousands; a lead of 0 or of four or more digits («0,125»), or a «,» decimal elsewhere, is a decimal point; otherwise («3,142») it reads both ways; a space before groups of exactly three digits («1 250») groups thousands unless the lead is 0 or the text lists numbers with bare spaces elsewhere (then both ways); a number that reads both ways with two different verdicts cannot be compared and is never a match; a vulgar fraction («½») and \\frac{a}{b} read as a/b, and a whole number before a proper fraction is a mixed number («3 1/2», «3½» = 3.5); number within 1% relative, 5% when approximate or the unit says «تقريب»; the LAST number of the written text that is not part of a date («عام ١٤٤٠», «١٤٤٠هـ»), a page («ص 48») or a reference («المثال 3», «س11», «2A») is the answer, and every number when there is no other; a written unit must match after normalization (Arabic full names alias the symbols: متر = م, سنتيمتر = سم, كيلومتر = كم, درجة = °, ثانية = ث, …; words aliased one by one are looked up again, «سنتيمترًا مربعًا» = سم²), a missing one is accepted; choice letters with أ/ب/ج/د = A–D; truth values, the FIRST truth word deciding, with the accusative and feminine forms («صحيحًا», «خاطئًا», «صائبة»; «صحيحة، لا يوجد مثال مضاد» is true; «لا» counts only as a whole reply or before a stop); text equal after normalization (diacritics, tatweel, hamza/alef, ة/ه, ى/ي, case, spaces, punctuation) or contained as whole words. Leak: a number leaks only at its exact value, never as an item label («2A»), a reference («السؤال 11») or a page, and only when the item's book text does not hold it; a text answer leaks only on a line announcing an answer («الإجابة», «الجواب», «الحل», «الناتج») or right after «=» («شوال = 10» in a numbered cycle is given data); choice and bool never leak.",
